components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-362-    /* Notes on implementation:
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-363-     *
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-364-     * 1) Note: ESP32-P4 CPU support overlapping PMP regions, configuration is based on static priority
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-365-     * feature (lowest numbered entry has highest priority).
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-366-     *
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-367-     * 2) ESP32-P4 supports 16 PMA regions so we use this feature to block the invalid address ranges.
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-368-     * However the entries are not sufficient to block all reserved memory ranges and the excluded sections are:
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-369-     *    a. Region between LP ROM and LP SRAM
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-370-     *    b. Region between LP peripherals and External flash (direct access)
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-371-     *    c. Region between External flash (direct access) and External RAM (direct access)
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-372-     *    d. Region between External RAM (direct access) and HP ROM (direct access)
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-373-     *    e. Region between HP ROM (direct access) and HP L2MEM (direct access)
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-374-     *
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-375-     * 3) We use combination of NAPOT (Naturally Aligned Power Of Two) and TOR (top of range)
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-376-     * entries to map all the valid address space, bottom to top. This leaves us with some extra PMP entries
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-377-     * which can be used to provide more granular access
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-378-     *
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-379-     * 4) Entries are grouped in order with some static asserts to try and verify everything is
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-380-     * correct.
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-381-     *
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-382-     * 5) For ESP32-P4's versions less than v3, no explicit permissions are specified in PMP (default all permissions) for following regions:
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-383-     * limited entries:
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-384-     *    a. External RAM
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-385-     *    b. LP ROM, LP Peripherals, LP SRAM
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-386-     *    c. External flash, External RAM, HP ROM, HP L2MEM (direct access)
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-387-     */
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-388-
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-389-    /* There are 4 configuration scenarios for SRAM
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-390-     *
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-391-     * 1. Bootloader build:
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-392-     *    - We cannot set the lock bit as we need to reconfigure it again for the application.
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-393-     *      We configure PMP to cover entire valid IRAM and DRAM range.
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-394-     *
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-395-     * 2. Application build with CONFIG_ESP_SYSTEM_MEMPROT enabled
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-396-     *    - We split the SRAM into IRAM and DRAM such that IRAM region cannot be written to
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-397-     *      and DRAM region cannot be executed. We use _iram_text_end and _data_start markers to set the boundaries.
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-398-     *      We also lock these entries so the R/W/X permissions are enforced even for machine mode
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-399-     *
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-400-     * 3. Application build with CONFIG_ESP_SYSTEM_MEMPROT disabled
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-401-     *    - The IRAM-DRAM split is not enabled so we just need to ensure that access to only valid address ranges are successful
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-402-     *      so for that we set PMP to cover entire valid IRAM and DRAM region.
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-403-     *      We also lock these entries so the R/W/X permissions are enforced even for machine mode
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-404-     *
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-405-     * 4. CPU is in OCD debug mode
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-406-     *    - The IRAM-DRAM split is not enabled so that OpenOCD can write and execute from IRAM.
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-407-     *      We set PMP to cover entire valid IRAM and DRAM region.
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-408-     *      We also lock these entries so the R/W/X permissions are enforced even for machine mode
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-409-     */
components/esp_hw_support/port/esp32p4/cpu_region_protect.c-410-    //
