arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-131-/****************************************************************************
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-132- * Name: up_cpu_start
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-133- *
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-134- * Description:
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-135- *   In an SMP configuration, only one CPU is initially active (CPU 0).
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-136- *   System initialization occurs on that single thread. At the completion of
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-137- *   the initialization of the OS, just before beginning normal multitasking,
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-138- *   the additional CPUs would be started by calling this function.
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-139- *
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-140- *   Each CPU is provided the entry point to its IDLE task when started.  A
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-141- *   TCB for each CPU's IDLE task has been initialized and placed in the
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-142- *   CPU's g_assignedtasks[cpu] list.  No stack has been allocated or
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-143- *   initialized.
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-144- *
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-145- *   The OS initialization logic calls this function repeatedly until each
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-146- *   CPU has been started, 1 through (CONFIG_SMP_NCPUS-1).
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-147- *
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-148- * Input Parameters:
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-149- *   cpu - The index of the CPU being started.  This will be a numeric
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-150- *         value in the range of one to (CONFIG_SMP_NCPUS-1).
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-151- *         (CPU 0 is already active)
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-152- *
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-153- * Returned Value:
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-154- *   Zero on success; a negated errno value on failure.
arch/risc-v/src/common/riscv_cpustart.c-155- *
